# Freenove 4WD Car Kit ESP32 — runtime + test suite.
# Partition: 448 KB LittleFS (partitions_4M_ota_trim.csv) = 112 blocks @ 4KB.
# 4KB-block LittleFS usage: ~46 blocks data + ~6 dir/superblock meta = ~52 blocks; ~60 free.
# DO NOT HAND-MAINTAIN A BLOCK BUDGET HERE.  The line that used to sit here read
# "~23 blk -> ~75/112 used, ~37 free. Still fits; verify on flash."  Both halves were wrong:
# gc-pause-bench was estimated at ~1 block and is 8, and the verification it asked for was never
# performed against the files that broke it.  The image reached 134 blocks and `make flash` died
# at LFS_ERR_NOSPC ([B576]).  `w3 make assemble` now MEASURES this after staging and prints
# "filesystem fits: N/CAP blocks" or warns with the overage -- read that, not a comment.
# Omitted vs S3 devkit: llip-server, rsa, dh_groups, rxrs_ai_overrides (redundant w/ r7rs).
# Conform = r7rs+rxrs+r5rs-pitfall. Extend = ll-extensions + lamblisp-tests.

# Core runtime
core/setup.scm
core/Compiler.scm
core/Lobs.scm
core/Terminal.scm
