rxrs/rxrs_srfi.scm

# Board-specific init
# THE NAME MATTERS: setup.scm loads `(string-append "setup-" lamb-board ".scm")`, so a board file
# staged WITHOUT the `setup-` prefix lands on the filesystem and is never loaded.  This target had
# exactly that for months -- the file shipped, sat there, and nothing read it, so the vehicle
# booted with no app-loop and its sonar and motors were never ticked [B625].  Every other target
# stages `boards/setup-<env>.scm`; this one was the outlier.
boards/setup-Freenove-4WD-Car-Kit-ESP32.scm

# ===========================================================================
# THE 4WD IS AN APPLICATION RUNNER, NOT A TEST TARGET (owner, 2026-09-23).
# ===========================================================================
# The generic conformance and perf suites are GONE from this image and future conf/perf work goes
# to the WROVER.  They were 58 blocks -- 43% of an image that no longer fit its own partition
# ([B576]: 134 blocks needed, 128 available, `make flash` dying at LFS_ERR_NOSPC).
#
# Removed: bench-runner (14 blk), lamblisp-tests (12), rxrs-tests (9), gc-pause-bench (8),
#          benchmarks (7), ncg-fusion-probe (4), r5rs-pitfall (3), pause_bench (1).
#
# WHY THE BOARD RATHER THAN THE SUITES.  A 4 MB part with a 512 KB filesystem cannot hold a
# general-purpose test rig AND the robot stack it exists to run -- behaviours, LEDs, sonar, the
# camera, the LLIP vision path and [P123] Part G's HUD sender.  Every block spent on a suite that
# runs identically on any board is a block unavailable to the one thing only THIS board can do.
# The WROVER has the space and no competing application.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT BREAK, checked rather than assumed:
#   * CONFORM/SMOKE/SUBSYSTEM/EXTEND are UNAFFECTED.  `_w3_run_correct_esp32` stages "runtime +
#     ONLY this test_id's files, uploadfs, reboot, THEN load the runner" -- the correctness tiers
#     never used the resident copies.  The three conformance files removed above were dead weight
#     in this image, carried since B65 and loaded from a per-tier stage in practice.
#   * PERF-EMBEDDED and GCPAUSE on this board DO break: their runners load from the resident FS.
#     That is intended -- the LX6 perf arena is `_W3_PERF_LX6`, which already defaults to WROVER,
#     so nothing scheduled by default targets the 4WD.  Anyone setting _W3_PERF_LX6=4WD explicitly
#     must re-add bench-runner/benchmarks/gc-pause-bench/pause_bench, and should expect the fit
#     check to tell them whether it still fits.
#
# WHAT STAYS, and it is not an exception to the rule.  `sonar-bench.scm` above is P126 R6's two
# sonar arms.  It measures THIS BOARD'S OWN HARDWARE and CANNOT move to the WROVER, which has no
# sonar -- so it is application-domain measurement, not a portable suite.  2 blocks.
#
# B65, MEASURED 2026-09-15 against the partition table this env ACTUALLY BUILDS WITH.
# All three of B65's missing files now ship.  They fit because the 4WD moved to the llloader
# layout in 7d90224 (2026-09-13): `partitions_4M_ota.csv` -- factory=llloader (1152 KB, the C
# recovery root), ota_0=the VM (2368 KB), storage=512 KB, and NO ota_1.  Dropping the OTA spare is
# what paid for all of it; that table's own header says the single-ota_0 layout "retires B65".
#
# THE FIRST PASS OF THIS NOTE WAS WRONG AND IS KEPT AS THE WARNING.  It concluded only two of the
# three could ship, from mklittlefs runs at `-s 0x070000` -- 448 KB, taken from
# `partitions_4M_ota_trim.csv` because B65's registry entry names that file.  NOTHING BUILDS WITH
# THAT TABLE.  No .ini and no board JSON references it; it is an orphan left behind by the move.
# The real slot is 0x080000.  Measuring carefully against the wrong geometry is not measuring.
#
# Verified at the REAL size (-p 256 -b 4096 -s 0x080000): image builds rc=0 with all three added.
# Re-run that before adding ANY file here, and take the size from platformio.ini's
# board_build.partitions for THIS env -- never from a registry entry or a comment, this one
# included.
# (rxrs-tests, lamblisp-tests, r5rs-pitfall removed 2026-09-23 -- see the header above.)

